Copyright (c) 2026 Neophronic Studios. All Rights Reserved.

NOTICE TO ALL FOUNDING MEMBERS, DEVELOPERS, AND CO-OWNERS:
This software, including its source code, database structures, application layout 
designs, AI prompt architectures, machine learning integrations, and financial/billing 
processing pipelines (collectively referred to as the "Software"), is the joint 
property of the founding members under the parent entity Neophronic Studios ("Company").

Access to this repository is restricted exclusively to authorized Co-Founders. 
By accessing, editing, or contributing to this codebase, all founding parties 
explicitly agree to the terms of intellectual property preservation and revenue 
distribution outlined below.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
1. PARENT COMPANY INTELLECTUAL PROPERTY & CODE VESTING
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
All right, title, and interest in and to the Software—including copyrights, 
patent rights, trademarks, and trade secrets—are owned collectively by the 
parent entity, Neophronic Studios. All code additions, framework updates, bug fixes, 
or backend architectures written by either Co-Founder instantly vest as the 
exclusive asset of the parent Company. No individual party holds personal 
copyrights to the codebase.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
2. FINANCIAL ARCHITECTURE & PROFIT-SHARING RULES
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
The Software is built upon a mutual subscription service model. All revenues 
generated by the platform shall be handled according to the following financial split:
a) OPERATIONAL COSTECTION: Before any profits are distributed to individual 
   co-founders, all primary business platform maintenance expenses—including but 
   not limited to Vercel hosting bills, OpenAI/Anthropic API usage bills, Stripe 
   payment processing transaction fees, and domain management costs—must be paid 
   in full from the gross revenue pool managed under Neophronic Studios.
b) PROFIT DISTRIBUTION: Net profits (all remaining cash flow after operating costs) 
   shall be distributed between the Co-Founders according to their mutually agreed 
   equity or dividend percentages. Disbursements shall occur on a regular monthly 
   basis unless otherwise agreed upon in writing.
c) GATEWAY TRANSPARENCY: Both Co-Founders must have full administrative visibility 
   into the connected payment gateway dashboard (e.g., Stripe, PayPal) linked to 
   Neophronic Studios to audit financial receipts, transaction histories, and 
   pending payouts fairly.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
3. RESTRICTIONS ON INDIVIDUAL CLONING & FORKING
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
To protect the shared valuation and financial health of the Company, no individual 
Co-Founder shall:
a) Copy, distribute, or host the source code via any personal public repository, 
   cloud bucket, or external server environment.
b) Use this repository or any portion of the Company's proprietary asset structure 
   to launch an independent, competing AI Studio or monetization platform.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
4. DISSOLUTION, SEPARATION & DEPARTURE PROTOCOL
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
In the event that a Co-Founder leaves the project, terminates their partnership, 
or transfers their business position:
a) The departing party's active access to this private repository and production 
   hosting server environments shall be revoked immediately for code protection.
b) The source code and platform intellectual property remain 100% with the surviving 
   parent entity, Neophronic Studios. 
c) Any buyout terms, ongoing revenue royalties, or equity distributions for the 
   departing member must be settled in a separate written corporate separation 
   agreement, based on their contributions up to the official date of separation.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
5. LIMITATION OF LIABILITY
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
THE SOFTWARE IS PROVIDED "AS IS", WITHOUT WARRANTY OF ANY KIND, EXPRESS OR 
IMPLIED. IN NO EVENT SHALL THE AUTHORS, CO-FOUNDERS, OR COPYRIGHT HOLDERS BE 
LIABLE FOR ANY CLAIM, DAMAGES, OR OTHER LIABILITY, WHETHER IN AN ACTION OF 
CONTRACT, TORT, OR OTHERWISE, ARISING FROM, OUT OF OR IN CONNECTION WITH THE 
SOFTWARE OR THE USE OR OTHER DEALINGS IN THE SOFTWARE.
